  "drawnOn": "A320",
  "from": "2023",
  "commemorates": "The Boston Bruins' centennial (1924-2024); JetBlue is the team's official airline.",
  "description": "Fuselage: black, with Bruins gold sweeping up from the belly behind the wing to the crown at the fin's root, edged with a thin white pinstripe; a narrow gold strip runs on forward along the lower fuselage to under the nose. Titles: 'jetBlue' in white over the forward windows; the gold Bruins centennial badge ('BRUINS 100 CENTENNIAL') over the windows ahead of the wing's trailing edge. Tail: gold fin carrying the Bruins' spoked B huge across it: a black ring round a white disc with gold spokes and the black B outlined in gold, cut by the leading edge. Engines black with 'jetblue.com' in white.",
