  "notes": "Measured on the right side: N632JB at Boston 2023-10-10, flipped and fitted; a left-side photo (2022-08-11) shows the fin the same. The gold's edge is a smooth sweep (three or four points would kink it), its white pinstripe about 0.1 m. The ring's foot over the fuselage by the stabilizer is clipped at the fin's root. 'Bear Force One' (small white script under the cockpit), the gold door outlines and the registration aren't drawn. The newest open photo is 2024-03-11; AirlineGeeks (2025-12-22) still counts the Bruins livery among JetBlue's Boston liveries."
